From: Mathias <mathias@pepservices.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov9282: keep control defaults inside updated ranges

__v4l2_ctrl_modify_range() rejects a default outside [min, max] with
-ERANGE before changing anything. Two range updates use fixed defaults
that short exposures and short frames push out of range:

- ov9282_update_exp_gain() narrows FLASH_DURATION to [0, exposure_us]
  with default OV9282_STROBE_FRAME_SPAN_DEFAULT (26). Any exposure under
  26 us (1-2 rows) makes the EXPOSURE s_ctrl fail with -ERANGE although
  the exposure registers were already written: every exposure update
  from userspace fails ("Unable to set control 0x00980911 (exposure):
  Numerical result out of range"), and an exposure set while the sensor
  is runtime-suspended (no s_ctrl, so it is committed) makes the
  __v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup() in enable_streams fail, so STREAMON
  returns -ERANGE.

- The VBLANK handler narrows EXPOSURE to [1, vblank + height - offset]
  with default OV9282_EXPOSURE_DEFAULT (642). Frames shorter than 667
  lines (640x400 at its minimum vblank) fail, the error is overwritten
  by the LPFR write, and the exposure limit stays at the previous frame
  length.

Clamp both defaults to the new maximum, and return the VBLANK range
error instead of dropping it.

---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov9282.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov9282.c
@@ -609,9 +609,16 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto error_release_group_hold;
 
+	/*
+	 * The strobe can't outlast the exposure. Short exposures (a few rows,
+	 * under OV9282_STROBE_FRAME_SPAN_DEFAULT us) must not move the default
+	 * outside the new range: that fails with -ERANGE, so the exposure
+	 * control was never committed and stream start failed.
+	 */
 	ret = __v4l2_ctrl_modify_range(ov9282->flash_duration,
 				       0, exposure_us, 1,
-				       OV9282_STROBE_FRAME_SPAN_DEFAULT);
+				       min_t(u32, exposure_us,
+					     OV9282_STROBE_FRAME_SPAN_DEFAULT));
 
 error_release_group_hold:
 	ret_hold = cci_write(ov9282->regmap, OV9282_REG_HOLD, 0, NULL);
@@ -653,6 +660,7 @@
 		container_of(ctrl->handler, struct ov9282, ctrl_handler);
 	u32 analog_gain;
 	u32 exposure;
+	u32 exposure_max;
 	u32 lpfr;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -664,12 +672,21 @@
 			ov9282->vblank,
 			ov9282->vblank + ov9282->cur_mode->height);
 
+		/*
+		 * Short frames (640x400 with a small vblank) give a maximum
+		 * below OV9282_EXPOSURE_DEFAULT; keep the default inside the
+		 * range, or the update fails with -ERANGE and the exposure
+		 * limit silently stays at the previous frame length.
+		 */
+		exposure_max = ov9282->vblank + ov9282->cur_mode->height -
+			       ov9282->variant->exposure_offset;
 		ret = __v4l2_ctrl_modify_range(ov9282->exp_ctrl,
 					       OV9282_EXPOSURE_MIN,
-					       ov9282->vblank +
-					       ov9282->cur_mode->height -
-					       ov9282->variant->exposure_offset,
-					       1, OV9282_EXPOSURE_DEFAULT);
+					       exposure_max, 1,
+					       min_t(u32, exposure_max,
+						     OV9282_EXPOSURE_DEFAULT));
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
 		break;
 	}
 
